`HostConnectionConfig.modelRoles` is `Map<String, String>` (String keys). In `hostModelPreset`:

```dart
taskSlots: {
 for (final entry in section.modelRoles.entries)
   if (TaskRole.all.contains(entry.key)) entry.key: entry.value,
},
``

`TaskRole.all.contains(entry.key)` — entry.key is a String. If `TaskRole` is an enum, `contains('smol')` is always FALSE (an enum value != string). But the test expects `preset.taskSlots == {TaskRole.smol: 'ain/ain_flash', TaskRole.subagent: 'ain/ain_pro'}`. So either TaskRole.all is a List<String> of ids, or TaskRole has custom ==/fromId. Let me check TaskRole.

Also `taskSlots` type: `Map<TaskRole, String>` presumably. The map literal `{entry.key: entry.value}` would need entry.key to be TaskRole. If TaskRole.all is `List<TaskRole>`, then `.contains(entry.key)` with String key — type error at compile? `List<TaskRole>.contains(Object?)` accepts any Object — returns false always for strings. Then the map literal would be `{String: String}` assigned to `Map<TaskRole, String>` — compile error. Unless TaskRole.all is List<String>.

The test compiles and passes (per PR evidence), so let me check TaskRole definition.

